# Unlike every 1-harness-sdk/* or 3-manual-instrumentation/* app, this
# folder has no main.py and no TRACE_TARGET switch -- docker-compose.yaml
# reads this file directly (both for its own ${VAR:-default}
# substitutions and, via env_file, as the litellm container's runtime
# environment). Local mode is the default: everything below except
# OPENAI_API_KEY can stay unset. To send traces to Harness Cloud & AI Cost
# Management instead, uncomment and fill in the three OTEL_* lines below.

# -------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider (OpenAI, routed by config.yaml's model_list)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# A real OpenAI key. There's no local-Ollama-style zero-cost path for
# this app the way 1-harness-sdk/openai/ has -- request.sh talks to the
# proxy over HTTP, and the proxy needs a real upstream to call.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Leave unset for a real OpenAI account (see config.yaml's comment on why
# leaving this line out entirely, not setting it to an empty value,
# matters). CI sets this to a stubbed server -- see
# .github/workflows/ci.yml's litellm-proxy job.
# OPENAI_API_BASE=

# -------------------------------------------------------------
# Harness (only needed to send traces to a real account instead of the
# bundled Jaeger -- uncomment all three)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# Proxy-specific var (LLD §11.2), not the standard OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_*
# name -- LiteLLM is documented to fall back to the standard vars if this
# one is unset, but every app in this repo sets its family's native var
# explicitly rather than relying on a fallback path.
# OTEL_ENDPOINT=https://prod3.harness.io/udp-ingest/otel

# Same x-harness-service-token / x-tenant-id pair every app in this repo
# sends (see docs/01-get-your-token.md) -- an ordinary personal/service
# account token; tenant validation applies to it normally, same as any
# other credential.
# OTEL_HEADERS=x-harness-service-token=<TOKEN>,x-tenant-id=<ACCOUNT_ID>

# harness.account.id is required here the same way it is for every other
# app (see docs/01-get-your-token.md) -- keep service.name alongside it,
# not as two separate variables, since this is the one place both are set.
# OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES=harness.account.id=<ACCOUNT_ID>,service.name=cacm-demo-litellm-proxy
